meta {
  name: 15 Return Sample
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/{{sampleId}}/return
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "handoverPerson": "Amit (courier)",
    "notes": "Returned to collector"
  }
}

tests {
  test("transition applied (or rejected by the state machine)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 201, 422]);
  });
}

docs {
  Return — **Accepted / Error / Stored → Returned**. Records `handoverPerson`
  (stored as the sample's `logisticsPerson`).

  Return of a receiving branch's accepted COPY sends the test back to its sender.
  **Cancelled order:** once the receiving branch has ACCEPTED its copy, the copy
  holds typed results, so it can no longer be sent back to the sender - refused
  with 422 `SAMPLE_ORDER_CANCELLED` (a group call with `skipInvalid` skips it with
  that reason) and nothing changes; Store then Discard stay open. Before Accept
  (transfer only Received) the receiving branch can still Reject / Repeat.

  **Back on the sender's own copy (Phase 2).** After the existing clear-down (values, notes, attachments and flags removed,
  report back to Pending) and the move back, the report points at the SENDER's Branch Master Data copy of the test again
  (`labTestId`) and `performingBranchLabTestId` is cleared (the order line's entry applies). A panel member's
  `memberBranchLabTestId` returns to the member entry it had. The sender's TAT clock restarts when it accepts the
  tube again. Still allowed only until a report has a validated result (Result Done, Approved, Published).
}
